/static/processed_images/**
/public

# Astro build output. `npm run build` emits dist/, but verification runs used
# dist-verifyN/ and friends; one rule covers the family.
/dist*/

# The scratch build the visual checks are served from. It is a build output
# under another name, and it is the same rule as the one above.
/.tmp-build/

node_modules/
.astro/

# Python leftovers from the generators
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.eggs/

# One-off scripts and audit artifacts from the Astro migration, all kept at the
# repo root with a leading underscore. The ones the build or the gates depend
# on stay tracked.
# (`python _audit_links_astro.py` gates the deploy; `_gen_redirects.py` writes
# the legacy-URL stubs in static/; `_gen_og.mjs` draws static/og.png, which is
# committed as a binary — the generator has to be in the repo to change it;
# `_gen_portrait.py` turns the ASCII portrait tool's page into
# src/data/portrait.ts.)
#
# `_legacy-urls.json` is the manifest of the legacy URLs: it is the list the
# link gate checks the built site against, so a clone that does not carry it
# runs the gate with that check silently switched off.
# `_verify_fixes.mjs` is the test runner the audit's fixes are verified with,
# and `_qa_server.mjs` is the static server those runs are served from.
/_*
!/_audit_links_astro.py
!/_gen_redirects.py
!/_gen_og.mjs
!/_gen_portrait.py
!/_legacy-urls.json
!/_verify_fixes.mjs
!/_qa_server.mjs

# The picture the portrait is drawn from. It stays on this machine: the
# source page is not in the repo, and only the map is committed. The
# generator is in the repo, so the map can be rebuilt from a new picture at
# any time.
/image.png

# A single-line HTML fragment an audit script dumped here. It looks like Markdown
# but is a slice of about.astro; src/pages/ is the source.
/ELEMENTS.md

# Local tooling / editor state
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
.claude-flow/
tmp/

# Agent notes that are not part of the site
QWEN.md
CLAUDE.md

# Secrets and logs
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
# Superpowers plan workspaces (ledger, briefs, review packages)
.superpowers/

# GStack tooling state: browse/probe logs, QA report runs, screenshot dumps
# and a copy of the built site. It is scratch space for the audit tooling, not
# part of the site.
/.gstack/

# Playwright MCP scratch: the page snapshots the browser tooling writes.
/.playwright-mcp/

# Redirect stubs that a real page has taken the address of. The address itself
# stays in _legacy-urls.json and docs/legacy-urls.txt; the file is scratch.
/.quarantine/

# The audit reports the QA tooling wrote. They are a working artifact of the
# audit, not site content; the fixes they asked for live in src/.
/docs/audit/
